WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
Taiwan's economy expanded nearly 13% in the second quarter, driven by AI demand and closer US links that are reshaping supply chains across the region. This is Omni View, episode 130. Official data showed Taiwan's economy grew nearly 13% in the second quarter, compared with a year earlier. The surge was tied to strong performance in artificial intelligence-related manufacturing and exports. The figures also reflect deeper supply chains

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:40.180
in integration with the United States. Nikkei Asia framed the result as evidence that US technology partnerships are delivering measurable gains for Taiwan's export sector.

00:00:41.080 --> 00:00:50.960
The same reporting highlighted how AI-driven demand is increasing Taiwan's exposure to global chip cycles and geopolitical tensions over semiconductor supply.

00:00:50.960 --> 00:01:05.960
Other regional coverage has noted that the growth coincides with continued US policy support for secure technology supply chains. The data come from government statistical agencies whose methods are reviewed by international bodies.

00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:12.140
Government releases indicate the expansion was concentrated in electronics and related components.

00:01:12.140 --> 00:01:24.240
Limited detail is yet available on performance in domestic services or agriculture. Interpretations differ on how sustainable the current pace remains if external demand softens.

00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:41.600
What happens next? Analysts will watch the third quarter numbers for signs of whether the electronics surge holds or narrows. Shifting now to a developing story in Ukraine. Ukrainian officials reported that Russian missile attacks on the capital killed at least 9 people.

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:56.580
The strikes used ballistic missiles and hit residential areas. Rescue operations continued through the night. BBC reporting described the attack as part of an escalation in Moscow's use of long-range weapons against Ukrainian cities.

00:01:56.580 --> 00:02:10.720
Ukrainian authorities have stated the strikes targeted civilian infrastructure. Russian statements have claimed military objectives. International monitoring groups continue to document civilian casualties in both countries.

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:20.580
The incident follows a pattern of repeated long-range strikes on the capital in recent weeks. Ukrainian air defense systems reported partial intercepts.

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:27.660
Local emergency services have described damage to apartment buildings and ongoing searches for additional victims.

00:02:28.360 --> 00:02:41.560
Next, a policy change affecting hundreds of thousands of people in the United States. The US government ended temporary protected status for approximately 350,000 Haitian and Syrian nationals.

00:02:41.560 --> 00:02:53.540
Families are now assessing limited legal pathways that rarely include return to their countries of origin. Local service organizations report increased demand for legal and housing assistance.

00:02:54.400 --> 00:03:03.760
The Christian Science Monitor has followed how community organizations in several US states are helping families navigate work permits and court backlogs.

00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:10.640
Federal agencies have cited changed security conditions in Haiti and Syria as the basis for the decision.

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:23.860
Advocacy groups have argued that many individuals still face documented risks if forced to leave. The policy change affects people who had been granted temporary status due to earlier instability.

00:03:23.860 --> 00:03:34.800
Many are now exploring asylum claims or other immigration routes. Service providers note that processing times for alternative legal options can extend for months or years.

00:03:35.540 --> 00:03:51.400
Meanwhile, in the Gulf region, Kuwait's army stated it destroyed hostile Iranian drones in its airspace. The drones were described as targeting several important sites. A government building and civilian property were hit, but no casualties were reported.

00:03:51.400 --> 00:04:03.400
France 24's live coverage placed the incident within a pattern of reported cross-border drone activity in the Gulf. Kuwait officials have emphasized that the response prevented further damage.

00:04:04.620 --> 00:04:16.620
Iranian authorities have not issued a public comment on the reported launch. The event occurred amid heightened regional tensions. Kuwait described the drones as hostile and aimed at infrastructure.

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:31.560
No further details on the origin or type of the drones have been released by Kuwaiti sources. Turning to business results from Japan. Sony reported a 32% jump in quarterly profit and raised its full year outlook.

00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:40.480
The company cited stronger sales in entertainment and electronics. The upgrade reflects performance through the first half of the fiscal year.

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:52.740
Nikkei Asia linked the result to continued demand for gaming and imaging products. Company filings show the gains were concentrated in segments less exposed to recent component shortages.

00:04:53.560 --> 00:05:09.400
The profit increase occurred alongside higher revenue in entertainment divisions, including music and film. Sony's updated guidance incorporates expectations for steady consumer spending on its core hardware and content lines through the remainder of the year.

00:05:09.400 --> 00:05:22.400
In technology developments, Chinese AI firm DeepSeek made the beta version of its V4 models available. The release comes as several companies compete on lower pricing for advanced systems.

00:05:23.460 --> 00:05:32.700
Early users are testing performance against existing offerings. Nikkei Asia reported that the move adds pressure on larger developers to adjust pricing.

00:05:32.700 --> 00:05:42.620
Industry observers note the models are being evaluated for both capability and cost efficiency. The beta launch follows earlier releases from the same company.

00:05:43.180 --> 00:05:55.320
It coincides with broader market efforts to reduce costs for large-scale AI training and inference. Users have begun comparing output quality and speed with models from established providers.

00:05:55.320 --> 00:06:06.980
Now, some progress worth knowing about. Japanese trading house Etochu announced a $1.9 billion investment in Tokyo centuries aircraft leasing division.

00:06:07.480 --> 00:06:15.540
The deal expands capacity in a sector recovering from earlier pandemic losses. Completion is expected later this year.

00:06:15.540 --> 00:06:26.900
Nikkei Asia noted the transaction will increase the combined fleet and leasing portfolio. The investment occurs against a backdrop of steady demand for commercial aircraft financing.

00:06:27.460 --> 00:06:33.780
Tokyo centuries existing operations include a range of leased aircraft serving airlines worldwide.

00:06:34.400 --> 00:06:40.920
The capital injection is intended to support fleet modernization and additional acquisitions in the coming years.

00:06:40.920 --> 00:06:53.860
Now, to really understand this story, there's something most coverage leaves out. Most coverage of a 13% GDP jump treats the number as a simple snapshot of overall economic health.

00:06:54.520 --> 00:07:07.740
In reality, GDP is assembled from detailed sectoral data that can be heavily influenced by one or two export-oriented industries whose output is measured through customs records and company filings.

00:07:07.740 --> 00:07:16.620
When AI chip demand rises sharply, the value of those exports is recorded at current prices and added to the national accounts.

00:07:17.380 --> 00:07:22.740
This produces a large percentage increase even if other parts of the economy grow modestly.

00:07:23.400 --> 00:07:31.960
This same accounting method explains why earlier technology cycles produce similar spikes followed by reversals when external demand changed.

00:07:31.960 --> 00:07:44.540
Taiwan's statistical agency releases both headline figures and component breakdowns. These allow analysts to isolate the contribution of electronics manufacturing from services or agriculture.

00:07:45.320 --> 00:07:54.580
When you hear claims that the economy is booming, you can check whether the growth is concentrated in a narrow set of industries whose fortunes depend on global buyers.

00:07:54.580 --> 00:08:07.920
One concrete step is to look at the statistical agency's own sector breakdown tables. These tables are released alongside headline GDP and show exactly which categories drove the change.

00:08:08.640 --> 00:08:16.740
They also include year-over-year comparisons that reveal whether the surge reflects sustained trends or temporary price and volume effects.

00:08:16.740 --> 00:08:26.720
Historical data from previous semiconductor cycles show that such concentrated gains can reverse within two or three quarters if buyer orders shift.

00:08:27.540 --> 00:08:35.140
If you want to go deeper on Taiwan's growth figures, compare how Nike Asia and other regional outlets are covering the same data release.

00:08:35.760 --> 00:08:43.680
Tomorrow, watch for further updates on rescue efforts in Kiev and any official response from Iranian authorities regarding the drone incident.

